# internOS project-level .gitignore
#
# Lives at a project root (e.g. `<workspace>/projects/<project>/.gitignore`).
# This file is for the PROJECT REPO — the one that lives at <org>/<project>
# on GitHub. The project repo tracks internOS state (PROJECT.md, AGENTS.md,
# POD.md, TICK.md, workstreams/, docs/) AND a `code/` container directory
# whose subdirectories are independent code repos.
#
# Allowlist style: ignore everything, then re-include the internOS file
# shapes plus the code/ container (but not its nested repos). Update when
# the framework adds a new project- or workstream-level file shape.

# Ignore everything at the project root by default.
/*

# Re-include the canonical project-level internOS files.
!/.gitignore
!/PROJECT.md
!/POD.md
!/TICK.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/README.md
!/docs/
!/workstreams/
!/code/

# tick.md tooling: re-include its config but not its runtime state.
!/.tick/
.tick/*
!.tick/config.yml

# Inside workstreams/, allowlist the canonical per-workstream files. Any
# scratch artifact, generated output, or nested code repo inside a workstream
# stays untracked unless explicitly re-included below.
workstreams/*/*
!workstreams/*/BRIEF.md
!workstreams/*/STATUS.md
!workstreams/*/MEMORY.md
!workstreams/*/DECISIONS.md
!workstreams/*/STAKEHOLDERS.md
!workstreams/*/RESOURCES.md
!workstreams/*/SESSIONS.md
!workstreams/*/ONBOARDING.md
!workstreams/*/README.md
!workstreams/*/docs/

# Inside code/, track the container's README and the derived worktree ledger.
# Each subdirectory is an independent git repo with its own remote and must
# remain opaque to this one. Git worktrees for parallel/agent code work live at
# code/.worktrees/<name>/ (linked worktrees of a code repo) and stay ignored by
# the `code/*` rule below — no extra line needed. WORKTREES.md is the derived
# ledger written by worktree.sh (like REGISTRY.md); track it.
code/*
!code/README.md
!code/WORKTREES.md
!code/.gitkeep
